1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.714
Welcome. In this beginner class, you will
separate five parts:

2
00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:11.429
model, application, retrieval, tool, and
agentic workflow. You will then

3
00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:17.143
test generated reminders against supplied
evidence, correct only conflicting claims,

4
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:22.857
and avoid guessing about hidden causes.
The central rule is

5
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:28.571
simple: useful generation is not automatic
evidence. By the end,

6
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:34.286
you should know when to verify, narrow, or
stop an

7
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:40.000
AI-assisted task.

8
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.294
Begin with the parts. A model is a
mathematical construct

9
00:00:45.294 --> 00:00:50.588
that processes input data and returns
output. In a language

10
00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:55.882
model, inputs and outputs are tokens,
which may be words,

11
00:00:55.882 --> 00:01:01.176
characters, or parts of words. A prompt is
text supplied

12
00:01:01.176 --> 00:01:06.471
to condition behavior, and inference is
when a trained model

13
00:01:06.471 --> 00:01:11.765
generates a response. A context window is
the finite number

14
00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:17.059
of tokens the model can process in a
prompt. An

15
00:01:17.059 --> 00:01:22.353
application is the larger product around
the model. It may

16
00:01:22.353 --> 00:01:27.647
connect an interface, files, policies,
retrieval, tools, and code. Retrieval

17
00:01:27.647 --> 00:01:32.941
locates stored material and supplies
selected material for use; the

18
00:01:32.941 --> 00:01:38.235
retrieved note remains the factual source.
Here, a tool means

19
00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:43.529
callable software that performs a defined
operation outside the model.

20
00:01:43.529 --> 00:01:48.824
An agent can plan and execute actions for
a user,

21
00:01:48.824 --> 00:01:54.118
while an agentic workflow can sequence
permitted steps, state, tools,

22
00:01:54.118 --> 00:01:59.412
feedback, and model-directed continuation.
Keep the labels separate: the model

23
00:01:59.412 --> 00:02:04.706
generates, the application coordinates,
retrieval locates, the tool operates, and

24
00:02:04.706 --> 00:02:10.000
the workflow sequences actions.

25
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.333
Generative systems can explain, summarize,
transform, classify, extract, compare,

26
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:20.667
brainstorm, translate, draft, write code,
and analyze supplied data. A

27
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:26.000
multimodal model accepts or produces more
than one modality, such

28
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.333
as images and text. These are task
categories, not guarantees

29
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:36.667
that every application supports them or
performs them correctly. Generated

30
00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:42.000
statements may be fabricated, stale,
broad, biased, inconsistent, or

31
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.333
unsupported. The glossary calls
plausible-seeming but factually incorrect

32
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:52.667
real-world output a hallucination. When
supplied evidence shows a mismatch

33
00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:58.000
but not its internal cause, use the
observable description unsupported

34
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.333
or conflicting statement. Do not infer
whether retrieval, prompting, generation,

35
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:08.667
code, or another detail caused it. Also,
models do not

36
